Feature: On-Time Delivery Analysis for Logistics Partners in Supply Chain

  This feature calculates on-time delivery percentages for logistics partners delivering critical medicines, identifies partners with perfect records, and flags those requiring improvement.

  Background:
    Given the table "purgo_playground.supply_chain_delivery" exists in Unity Catalog
    And the table contains columns: Shipment_ID (string), Logistics_Partner (string), Delivery_Status (string), Medicine_ID (string), Country_Name (string), Category_Wise (string), Revenue (bigint), Manufacture_Date (date), Warehouse (string), Stock (bigint), Reorder_Level (bigint), Expiry_Date (date), Unit_Cost (double), Batch_ID (string)
    And 'Critical_Medicines' is defined as the literal value 'Critical_Medicines' in the Category_Wise column
    And a delivery is considered "On-Time" if Delivery_Status equals 'On-Time'
    And only rows with non-null values in required columns (Category_Wise, Logistics_Partner, Delivery_Status, Shipment_ID) are considered valid
    And if any required field is null, the row is excluded from aggregation
    And analysis is performed at the level of (Category_Wise, Logistics_Partner) grouping

  Scenario: Happy Path - Successful Calculation and Segregation of Perfect and Underperforming Partners
    Given the table contains at least one row with Category_Wise = "Critical_Medicines"
    And at least two distinct Logistics_Partner values
    When the system filters rows where Category_Wise = "Critical_Medicines"
    And groups the data by Category_Wise and Logistics_Partner
    And counts On_Time_Count as the number of rows with Delivery_Status = "On-Time"
    And counts Total_Shipments as the total number of shipments for each Logistics_Partner
    And calculates On_Time_Percentage as (On_Time_Count divided by Total_Shipments) multiplied by 100, rounded to 2 decimal places
    Then the result output includes the columns: Category_Wise, Logistics_Partner, On_Time_Count, Total_Shipments, On_Time_Percentage
    And partners where On_Time_Percentage = 100 are included in perfect_partners_df
    And partners where On_Time_Percentage < 100 are included in underperforming_partners_df

  Scenario Outline: Data-Driven Test for Perfect, Underperforming, and Missing Data Partners
    Given the table contains the following rows:
      | Shipment_ID | Logistics_Partner | Delivery_Status | Category_Wise      |
      | S1         | PartnerA          | On-Time         | Critical_Medicines |
      | S2         | PartnerA          | On-Time         | Critical_Medicines |
      | S3         | PartnerB          | Delayed         | Critical_Medicines |
      | S4         | PartnerB          | On-Time         | Critical_Medicines |
      | S5         | PartnerC          | On-Time         | Non_Critical       |
      | S6         | PartnerC          | Delayed         | Critical_Medicines |
      | S7         |                    | On-Time         | Critical_Medicines |
      | S8         | PartnerD          |                 | Critical_Medicines |
    When the analysis is performed
    Then for Logistics_Partner "<Partner>", On_Time_Count is <on_time>, Total_Shipments is <total>, On_Time_Percentage is <percent>
    And if On_Time_Percentage = 100, the partner is in perfect_partners_df
    And if On_Time_Percentage < 100, the partner is in underperforming_partners_df
    And rows with missing Logistics_Partner or Delivery_Status are excluded from calculation

    Examples:
      | Partner  | on_time | total | percent |
      | PartnerA | 2       | 2     | 100.00  |
      | PartnerB | 1       | 2     | 50.00   |
      | PartnerC | 0       | 1     | 0.00    |

  Scenario: Error Case - No Critical Medicines in Dataset
    Given the table contains only rows where Category_Wise != "Critical_Medicines"
    When the analysis is performed
    Then the result output is an empty dataframe with columns: Category_Wise, Logistics_Partner, On_Time_Count, Total_Shipments, On_Time_Percentage
    And both perfect_partners_df and underperforming_partners_df are empty

  Scenario: Error Handling - Missing Required Columns
    Given the table definition is missing one or more of the following columns: Category_Wise, Logistics_Partner, Delivery_Status, Shipment_ID
    When the analysis is attempted
    Then the system raises an error "Missing required columns: [<MissingColumnName>]" and halts the computation

  Scenario: Error Handling - Null or Blank Required Fields in Any Row
    Given one or more rows have null or blank values in Category_Wise, Logistics_Partner, Delivery_Status, or Shipment_ID
    When the analysis is performed
    Then such rows are excluded from On_Time_Count and Total_Shipments aggregation
    And the final result does not count these rows towards any partner's statistics

  Scenario: Data Validation - Delivery_Status Non-standard Values
    Given the table contains Delivery_Status values other than "On-Time" and "Delayed"
    When the analysis is performed
    Then only rows with Delivery_Status = "On-Time" are counted towards On_Time_Count
    And all other statuses are included in Total_Shipments but not in On_Time_Count

  Scenario Outline: On-Time Percentage Calculation Validation (Edge Cases)
    Given the table has the following data:
      | Logistics_Partner | Category_Wise      | Delivery_Status |
      | PartnerX          | Critical_Medicines | On-Time         |
      | PartnerX          | Critical_Medicines | Delayed         |
      | PartnerX          | Critical_Medicines | Lost            |
      | PartnerY          | Critical_Medicines | On-Time         |
      | PartnerY          | Critical_Medicines | On-Time         |
    When the calculation for On_Time_Percentage is performed on <Partner>
    Then On_Time_Count is <on_time>
    And Total_Shipments is <total>
    And On_Time_Percentage is <percent>

    Examples:
      | Partner  | on_time | total | percent |
      | PartnerX | 1       | 3     | 33.33   |
      | PartnerY | 2       | 2     | 100.00  |

  Scenario: Output Data Format Validation
    Given the analysis was successful
    When the result dataframe is output
    Then each row includes columns: Category_Wise (string), Logistics_Partner (string), On_Time_Count (bigint), Total_Shipments (bigint), On_Time_Percentage (double)
    And On_Time_Percentage is always rounded to two decimal places
    And partners are split into perfect_partners_df (On_Time_Percentage = 100) and underperforming_partners_df (On_Time_Percentage < 100)

  Scenario: Recommendation for Alternative Partner
    Given at least one Logistics_Partner has On_Time_Percentage = 100
    And at least one partner has On_Time_Percentage < 100
    When analysis is complete
    Then the system recommends switching underperforming partners to any partner(s) in perfect_partners_df for critical medicines delivery

  Scenario: No Shipments/Zero Denominator Scenario
    Given a partner has zero shipments in the dataset for Category_Wise = "Critical_Medicines"
    When the analysis is performed
    Then the partner does not appear in the final output result

  Scenario: Strict Data Consistency Checks
    Given shipment IDs are not unique or Logistics_Partner string fields contain whitespace-only
    When the analysis runs
    Then such rows are excluded from the result set
    And only valid, distinct shipments with non-blank partner names are counted

  # Validation Rules Summary (Technical)
  # - Category_Wise == "Critical_Medicines" (case-sensitive match)
  # - Only Delivery_Status == "On-Time" counts as on time
  # - Null or blank values in any required columns -> row excluded from result
  # - Output column types: (Category_Wise: string, Logistics_Partner: string, On_Time_Count: bigint, Total_Shipments: bigint, On_Time_Percentage: double [rounded 2 decimals])
  # - On_Time_Percentage = (On_Time_Count / Total_Shipments) * 100, 0 if denominator is zero

  Scenario: Validate Error Message for No Table Access
    Given user does not have access permissions to table "purgo_playground.supply_chain_delivery"
    When the analysis job attempts to read the table
    Then the system raises an error containing the message "Permission denied" or "Access denied to Unity Catalog table"

